# REPRODUCTION for bead inc-akac, rebuilt by inc-b4l3g.2: a summoned frost giant
# (lib/mon2.irh, ABILITY(CA_FEED_UPON_PAIN,6)) is a level-6 source of Feed upon
# Pain. It lands blows on a LOADED player (INCURSION_LOAD=
# tools/fixtures/chars/orc-priest-pain-seed1-sneakopts.sav) who only waits. The
# priest is the target because he does not hide: a hiding rogue goes unseen, so
# the giant never attacks. Read with tools/check_feed_upon_pain.sh via
# logs/pain.log (INCURSION_PAIN_PROBE=1). One giant is summoned beside the
# player (its 3x3 body may be nudged to any side, so the script never attacks
# it). Everything else is genocided first. The check sets
# INCURSION_SUMMON_NO_GEAR=1, so the giant has no gear and its blow is fixed.
# '.' (rest) is the wait: 's' opened a "What do you want to push?" prompt, which
# turned every later wait into a no-op.
w
@choose "Genocide Everything"

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Giants"
@choose "frost giant"
RIGHT ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

@dump:victim

.
@while "Die?" n
@dump:t01
.
@while "Die?" n
@dump:t02
.
@while "Die?" n
@dump:t03
.
@while "Die?" n
@dump:t04
.
@while "Die?" n
@dump:t05
.
@while "Die?" n
@dump:t06

@quit
